  mg/dL, respectively. Clinical outcome measurements included the National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale at the     
  end of infusion, at 24 hours, and at discharge. Potential complications from caffeine and ethanol were recorded.      
  Cases were reviewed by an independent stroke neurologist for safety. RESULTS A total of 23 patients were recruited.   
  Target blood caffeine and ethanol levels were reached in 0 of the 4 patients in the first group. The second dose      
